    "claim_boundary": "Default BiRRF weights and smoothing are engineering defaults copied from rank-fusion practice. Identical or highly correlated, substantially overlapping KG rank orders are collapsed to one effective vote to prevent duplicate evidence counting. Candidate-level branches that declare a shared correlation group are also capped to one effective vote; missing lineage remains explicit and may be configured as a blocking conflict. When an expected fault universe is explicitly frozen, the coverage guard consumes a content-addressed executable-evidence declaration rather than an episode candidate list. Incomplete capability may suppress a KG branch or, only under an explicit experimental policy, attenuate its weight by structural coverage. This prevents sparse knowledge from asymmetrically overriding unsupported data-branch faults without discarding the possibility of development-validated partial-coverage fusion. These controls are not calibrated for flight diagnosis.",
